<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bohechío</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 1500</span> · <a href="/centuries/15th-century">15th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bohechío was the paramount cacique of Jaragua in south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispaniola">Hispaniola</a> when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a> arrived, ruling from a town near modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leogane">Léogâne</a> and receiving tribute from many lesser chiefs. He received Bartholomew Columbus in 1497 and agreed to pay tribute in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cassava">cassava</a> bread rather than gold, which his land lacked. On his death his sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anacaona">Anacaona</a> succeeded him.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bohechio.jpg" alt="Bohechío" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Estalincastillo · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pueblo_de_Bohechio.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
